{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Detection rules for Unity hot-update frameworks (WP5b). Every signal carries `sources`; signals whose facts could not be checked against an upstream source are flagged `unverified` and are down-weighted by the detector. Signal types: namespace (metadata/dump namespace, segment-wise prefix), type (exact metadata identifier), assembly (exact assembly file name in the metadata string pool), native_regex / native_literal (bytes searched in the unencrypted parts of Mach-O binaries), file (regex on the app-relative path, case-insensitive), pool_regex (case-insensitive regex on a metadata identifier).",
